/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/QC/reports/metered-usage-rating-pipeline/v2.md:200:- TS-24 ✅ v1 G03-3 fixed. `_run` test_output.py:1195-1203 starts the program with `start_new_session=True` under `_RUN_LOCK`, and `_reap` :1225-1240 kills the process group, then (as root) sweeps every live process of uid `nobody` up to 100 rounds, then kills/collects the child. Since agent code runs only as `nobody` (setpriv :35) and cannot change uid, a `setsid` daemon is caught by the uid sweep; `/logs/verifier` is root:root 755 (test.sh) so even a survivor could not write reward.json. Probe (/tmp/oracle-qc/metered-usage-rating-pipeline-20261029T061854-e0a7/g03/: transform.py forks, `setsid`, double-forks, points fds at /dev/null, then either sleeps 6 s or fork-hops for 6 s, then writes /tmp/survivor-*; drive.py calls `_run` in the warm verifier image as root with /tests go-rwx): 3 of 3 containers `plain rc 0 run+reap 0.03s left: []`, `hop rc 0 run+reap 0.07s left: []`, no survivor file after 9 s. `_RUN_LOCK` keeps the sweep from killing a concurrent check's run.
